===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|burjon}}, {{m|enm|burioun||shoot, bud}}, from {{der|en|xno|burjun}}, {{m|fro|burgeon}}, {{m|fro|burgon}} (compare {{cog|fro|burjon||a bud}}), from Old {{der|en|frk|*burjo||sprout, offshoot, descendant}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*burjô||sprout, descendant, offshoot}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*burjaną||to raise up}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰrē-||to bear}}. Compare {{cog|goh|burjan||to push up, raise}}, {{cog|ang|byrian||to come up, occur}}, {{cog|ang|byre||child, son, descendant}}, {{cog|sq|buron||sprout, spring, gush out}}. More at {{l|en|bear}}.

Alternate etymology derives {{der|en|fro|burjon||bud}} from {{der|en|VL.|*burrionem}}, accusative of {{m|la|*burrio}}, from {{der|en|LL.|burra||wool, fluff}} (presumably from the down covering certain buds).

